// Storing a borrow of 'a into a place that holds 'b borrows: nothing says 'a
// outlives 'b, so the store is refused.
//
// Verdict: refuse, ErrorEscape at the store (written first as ErrorInvType,
// a guess; a borrow stored where it may not live is ErrorEscape).
// Basis: language rule (1 Oct 2026) -- a borrow of one named lifetime may not
// be stored inside a place of another, because nothing guarantees their
// relative lifetimes. (With a where clause saying 'a outlives 'b it is
// allowed: lifetime_band_where_store_longer.)
// Master d331baab: refused at parse ('a read as a loop label). Stage 6 fixed
// it.

mod lifetime_band_named_store_without_where;

fn st(dst &mut &'b i64, src &'a i64) {
  *dst = src;                //~ ErrorEscape
}
